      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The hardest ACT items touch matrices, vectors, logarithms and the imaginary unit \\( i \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Advanced topics",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( i^{2}=-1 \\); add matrices entrywise; a vector \\( (a,b) \\) has magnitude \\( \\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}} \\); \\( \\log_b x=y \\) means \\( b^{y}=x \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Imaginary",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( i^{2}=-1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Matrix",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "add entrywise",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Vector",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Logarithm",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\log_b x \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Simplify \\( i^{2}+i^{4} \\). \\[ -1+1=0. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Complex Numbers & Polar Form",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A complex number \\(z = a+bi\\) has modulus \\(|z| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\\) and argument \\(\\theta = \\arctan(b/a)\\). Polar form: \\(z = r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta)\\). Multiplying in polar: multiply moduli, add arguments.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Matrix determinant & inverse",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find \\(A^{-1}\\) for \\(A = \\begin{pmatrix}3&1\\\\5&2\\end{pmatrix}\\). <p>\\(\\det A = 6-5 = 1\\). \\(A^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{1}\\begin{pmatrix}2&-1\\\\-5&3\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}2&-1\\\\-5&3\\end{pmatrix}\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Simplify \\((2+3i)(1-i)\\) and write in the form \\(a+bi\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\((2+3i)(1-i) = 2 - 2i + 3i - 3i^2 = 2 + i + 3 = 5+i\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
